\section{Curvature--Information Duality}

Curvature invariants are functionals of informational gradients:
\begin{equation}
R = c_1 \Box \rho_I + c_2 (\partial \rho_I)^2,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
C^2 = d_1 (\partial \partial \rho_I)^2 + d_2 (\partial \rho_I)^4,
\end{equation}
where $R$ is the Ricci scalar and $C^2$ is the Weyl curvature invariant.